course: dictionary
lesson: 4958
title: The Inca
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Inca were a people who lived in the Andes mountains of South America. Their empire had its capital at Cusco, in what is now Peru. Write Inca with a capital I, because it is a name.
explain: Inca can be a noun for the people: «the Incas built roads through the mountains». It can be a noun for their ruler, the emperor. It can also be an adjective that describes things, as in «the Inca Empire» or «Inca gold».
explain: Use the words around Inca to work out its job. In «the Inca Trail», the word trail tells you Inca describes a path. Ask yourself: is it a people, a ruler, or a thing made by them?
fact: The Inca were a people of the Andes mountains in South America.
fact: Their empire had its capital at Cusco, in today's Peru.
fact: The Inca built Machu Picchu and about 40,000 km of roads, some with rope bridges.
fact: Their stone walls fit so exactly that a knife blade cannot fit between the stones.
fact: They spoke Quechua, which millions of people still speak today.
exercise: What does Inca mean in «the Inca Empire»? | A mountain in Italy | *A great empire of the Andes, ruled by the Inca | A kind of potato | A ship from Spain
exercise: The Inca were a people of which mountains? | The Himalayas | *The Andes | The Alps | The Rockies
exercise: Which city was the capital of the Inca Empire? | Machu Picchu | Lima | *Cusco | Quito
test: Why is Inca written with a capital letter? | It is a verb | It is at the start of a sentence every time | *It is a name | It is a colour
test: Which language did the Inca people speak, and millions still speak today? | Latin | Spanish | French | *Quechua
exam: Which fact about the Inca is true? | They wrote books on paper | *They built stone walls so exact that a knife blade cannot fit between the stones | They lived in Europe | They had horses and carts with wheels
